endencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducable in Godot 4.5rc2\n- Reproducable in Godot 4.5-beta1\n- Not reproducable in Godot 4.4.1\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.rc2 - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 4 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 6900 XT (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 32.0.21013.1000) - AMD Ryzen 9 5900X 12-Core Processor (24 threads) - 31.92 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nI use the `InterVariable` font in the Editor:\n\n<img width=\"874\" height=\"363\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9169c603-2cd1-4e12-833d-d090e625abb6\" />\n\nSince the Godot 4.5-beta1 version, the font looks a bit blurry compared to Godot 4.4.1:\n\n<img width=\"365\" height=\"264\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4634c32b-17b8-4a6c-84c3-bcd1123ba48c\" />\n\nI don't know if this might be expected, but I thought I report this in case it might be a font rendering regression.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Set the `InterVariable` font. \n  - Can be downloaded from the Inter Repo: https://github.com/rsms/inter/releases/tag/v4.1\n- Edit a `Node2D` in the Godot Editor\n- The font looks different compared to Godot 4.4.1, and a bit blurry\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nToo simple to reproduce, and font must be changed in the editor settings (so not project related)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}"